 <aside id="notes" hidden><button id="close-notes" aria-label="Close study notes">×</button><h2>Cloth, leather & iron.</h2><p>A worn cap, rolled shirt sleeves, an open waistcoat and a leather apron reflect the clothing in our chainmaking references.</p><p>This is an interpreted worker for the 1865 village, not an identified resident. The generated figure and its repaired clothing are an interpretation; they do not establish an exact likeness or date.</p><p>The study uses one existing forge workstation. The tongs hold a link on the anvil while the hammer lifts, strikes and settles.</p><a href="/chainmaker-v2/chainmaker.glb" download>Download the figure ↓</a></aside>
